meta {
  name: Login
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
  body: formUrlEncoded
  auth: inherit
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  email: user3@gmail.com
  password: 12345678
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Login
  
  Authenticates a user with their email and password. On success, sets `cedaraccess` and `cedarrefresh` HTTP-only cookies on the response.
  
  ## Authorization
  None — this is a public endpoint.
  
  ## Request Body (`form-urlencoded`)
  
  | Field    | Type   | Required | Constraints                                        |
  |----------|--------|----------|----------------------------------------------------|
  | email    | string | Yes      | Must be a valid email. Stored as lowercase/trimmed. |
  | password | string | Yes      | Minimum 8 characters.                              |
  
  ## Response
  Returns the authenticated user object. Access and refresh tokens are set as HTTP-only cookies (`cedaraccess`, `cedarrefresh`).
  
  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — Validation failed (missing/invalid fields).
  - `404 Not Found` — Invalid credentials (wrong email or password).
  - `429 Too Many Requests` — Rate limit exceeded (`authLimiter`: 5 requests per 15-minute window, keyed by IP).
  
  ## Rate Limiting
  This endpoint is protected by `authLimiter` — a maximum of **5 requests per 15-minute window**, keyed by the client's IP address. Exceeds return a `429` with `{ code: "RATE_LIMITED", message: "Too many login attempts. Please try again later." }`.
}
